      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should be good with this.\nI know, that Java code can use PUBLIC even for RPA addresses, but this is something we handle in btif_gatt_client\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/btif/src/btif_gatt_client.cc;l\u003d290;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1?q\u003dbtif_gatt_c\n\nWhat is happening there, we look into bt_config.conf if Java used PUBLIC and make sure that this match the address type we have there.\n\nIf device is known, we overwrite the type.\n\nThis code is looking into security record which is another state.\n\nSo what is happening here, if this function is called for the device which is unknown for us, we just use provided address type - which seems to be fine.\n\nbtw: in the comment here: https://b.corp.google.com/issues/278199753#comment5, I showed logs for the case where Java calls connect using pseudo address (which is RPA but used with type PUBLIC)",
